#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105541 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6c58537-344e-5842-b68c-d9b5a9d7ca96" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "fc5fc31e-f585-5d15-8a8a-eb0d19704e9a" :question/math-academy-id "e-2947" :question/problem "Find the area of the triangle $\\triangle ABC.$\n\n![](images/f8/f892cd084f548769fa6b7352fece0e1aef3a66a4ab517ed5b5243d89041ac3a9.png)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = \\dfrac{b \\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =AB \\\\  & =AH+HB \\\\  & =6+3 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is\n\n$$\nh={CH} = 4 .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 4}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{2} \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105542 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6445834c-7788-5427-a72c-30b06cc8e6ab" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of an Isosceles Right Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "cdb1d145-6e8a-5213-a7f7-8076440cbbeb" :question/math-academy-id "e-2949" :question/problem "What is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown below?\n\n![](images/3b/3b68fc0b5c128122e7316db08e34932393db5bf557ffd889fd785265b758b447.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since $m\\angle{A}=m\\angle{C},$ we have an isosceles triangle, where $AB=BC.$\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {8}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105543 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Base or the Height of a Triangle Given Its Area"}] :question/id #uuid "58e1ce31-f6fc-5900-ab89-e00241045b12" :question/math-academy-id "e-2950" :question/problem "Consider the triangles $\\triangle ABC$ and $\\triangle CDE$ shown below. If the area of $\\triangle CDE$ is $25 \\textrm{ cm}^2,$ find the area of $\\triangle ABC.$\n\n![](images/bd/bd9840fd674fe7bf7b4f428591dfc6e9fbbaec8387836ece34694d17eaabe65b.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider $\\triangle CDE.$ We can see that $\\overline{CD}$ is the height corresponding to the base $\\overline{DE}$ and that $DE=10\\textrm{ cm}.$ \n\nSince the area of $\\triangle CDE$ is $25\\textrm{ cm}^2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 25 & =\\frac{10\\cdot CD}{2} \\\\ 25 & =5\\cdot CD \\\\ CD & =5\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that $\\overline{CD}$ is also the height of $\\triangle ABC$ corresponding to the base $\\overline{AB}.$\n\n![](images/ea/ea7f44b91e87a42029c5f00aae97a2eebf2e472ff890d4b91f4973e1e383e5c7.png)\n\nTherefore, we find the area of $\\triangle ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{AB\\cdot CD}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5}{2} \\\\  & =15{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Base or the Height of a Triangle Given Its Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41f96e27-bdd7-5af5-85cd-a7d4cae8cf15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508488} {:answer/id #uuid "4522ce6c-ceb2-59af-8de1-031e99eb3fcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508491} {:answer/id #uuid "59d1971b-9d87-547d-b44e-e2249b87b679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508522} {:answer/id #uuid "aebe24a0-a982-5e43-ac8e-d6f9ef609c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508654} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a4eb50-2a30-58e7-a4c5-d6f5478d5a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59d1971b-9d87-547d-b44e-e2249b87b679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508522} :answer-field/id #uuid "b79f9a3f-6b08-5799-b574-1481f53da89e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "efe752cf-6c60-5a23-aae8-55bc453cac9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-117368" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b66dea0994329cf63ff08137293efc33fe994a5ae0395d661dc014044a1c0d14.png)\n\nConsider the triangles $△ABC$ and $△CDE$ shown above. If the area of $△CDE$ is $27{\\text{ cm}}^{2}$, find the area of $△ABC.$\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider $△CDE.$ We can see that $\\overset{―}{CD}$ is the height corresponding to the base $\\overset{―}{DE}$ and that $DE=6\\text{ cm}.$ \n\nSince the area of $△CDE$ is $27{\\text{ cm}}^{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 27 & =\\frac{6\\cdot CD}{2} \\\\ 6CD & =54 \\\\ CD & =9\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that $\\overset{―}{CD}$ is also the height of $△ABC$ corresponding to the base $\\overset{―}{AB}.$\n\n![](images/95/95e84873b1353e6a04bb4e6e7df5f45c09eb4751b1170d6eaf8a9bcfa4b572de.png)\n\nTherefore, we find the area of $△ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{AB\\cdot CD}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 9}{2} \\\\  & =18{\\text{ cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6c58537-344e-5842-b68c-d9b5a9d7ca96" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6f74edc-39f7-5577-9d11-30854b64a223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6f74edc-39f7-5577-9d11-30854b64a223" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508756} :answer-field/id #uuid "04ecb164-1b59-540d-9f7b-f7200e5ea844" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c171c6db-2b08-53c8-ae94-2e1ffe80b16e" :question/math-academy-id "q-171954" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f2c8ddcb1cddce59fbecf25ea606e8400d04d896dfdb263dd0aaf4e6c7de682f.png)\n\nThe area of the triangle $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}\n${cm}^{2}.$\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the triangle is defined as \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is \n\n$$\nb=AB=12\\,\\text{cm}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is \n\n$$\nh=6\\,\\text{cm}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cdot 6}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{72}{2} \\\\  & =36\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508991 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Base or the Height of a Triangle Given Its Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00382e30-a564-55e8-904d-5fcee95e154d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.5\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508389} {:answer/id #uuid "2d63a2ed-5ba5-5201-bbcd-120a70c032c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.2\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508457} {:answer/id #uuid "4e8497f6-7f80-528c-9ccc-fe05a60dca49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.8\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508506} {:answer/id #uuid "54b437df-237e-5cbe-901f-e3dec8ac46ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508514} {:answer/id #uuid "fc8aa577-1c0d-575c-ac59-74c578543ac8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54b437df-237e-5cbe-901f-e3dec8ac46ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508514} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6c4c9c5-20e2-5ad2-b45c-aab945f75318" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e5a09c22-28d0-55d4-9b16-abdb75945ec5" :question/math-academy-id "q-21055" :question/problem "![](images/b1/b12eaaaf9aafa591bef00ca1b11d24783fae4a46f7253bddb05b9b206dbcb9e6.png)\n\nFind $HB$ given that the area of $△ABC$ is $140\\,{m}^{2},$  $AH=15\\,m,$ and $CH=14\\,m.$\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the triangle is defined as \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is $b=AB,$ and the corresponding height is \n\n$$\nh=CH=14\\,m.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the formula for the area, we can solve for the base as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 140 & =\\frac{b\\cdot 14}{2} \\\\ 280 & =b\\cdot 14 \\\\ b & =\\frac{280}{14} \\\\ b & =20\\,m\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $AB=20\\,m$ and hence, we have\n\n$$\nHB=AB-AH=20-15=5\\,m.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508965 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6c58537-344e-5842-b68c-d9b5a9d7ca96" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d17b541-3b1e-5cad-8b55-90c653d704ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508502} {:answer/id #uuid "98f0d08c-fbce-51d0-be7d-b549e908a1ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508620} {:answer/id #uuid "a5b4c832-5b2a-5c57-93d5-64555490cd2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508638} {:answer/id #uuid "c49b086b-700a-59dd-9be4-a6fcd55efb2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508694} {:answer/id #uuid "def9d678-fcf0-5088-bf30-db47e355c75b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d17b541-3b1e-5cad-8b55-90c653d704ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508502} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8b73006-e09d-58b6-a70a-2960668f8428" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a56eecfc-87ce-57b1-87a4-1fa356b28d07" :question/math-academy-id "q-53149" :question/problem "![](images/f6/f6b58865cc7048560bc547ed03b95977d5f9ed013cb411991a82d7da140717f7.png)\n\nFind the area of the triangle $△ABC.$\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the triangle is defined as \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is \n\n$$\nb=AC=5\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is\n\n$$\nh=BC=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 8}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{2} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354593 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6445834c-7788-5427-a72c-30b06cc8e6ab" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of an Isosceles Right Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01a966f4-dbc7-5e7f-b5c3-6801e6e0fd63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351579} {:answer/id #uuid "078fe28f-b6f9-59e7-baa7-6f94535bdc55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351633} {:answer/id #uuid "1ce73c74-b0aa-5831-857d-258578d42122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351825} {:answer/id #uuid "43cc795c-8aa7-515c-bcc6-e9198bafacc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352189} {:answer/id #uuid "67484ca0-9ae4-56cc-8e1f-cda96489e093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67484ca0-9ae4-56cc-8e1f-cda96489e093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352485} :answer-field/id #uuid "acc38aa9-2f81-50eb-be6b-41072cd0d10e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b779fa51-4da1-5c93-b91d-35c3acfc0806" :question/math-academy-id "q-87801" :question/problem "![](images/f1/f18be4b42008423fe08b165fea4b3807b247813112b92a6ad0932c07a33ba8b6.png)\n\nWhat is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Since $m∠A=m∠C$, we have an isosceles triangle, where $AB=BC.$\n\nHence, the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {4}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354594 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6445834c-7788-5427-a72c-30b06cc8e6ab" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of an Isosceles Right Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0663bea7-12f5-5928-84d7-bc207c70bfaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351623} {:answer/id #uuid "3101c5fb-53ba-5942-ad43-1ae35079f738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352018} {:answer/id #uuid "7e914068-1f39-55f3-a988-748244647a92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352677} {:answer/id #uuid "8150fcea-b946-540d-b0fd-6ae56c257637" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352692} {:answer/id #uuid "aa336a88-ddef-5077-bcae-4e7bf818c424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3101c5fb-53ba-5942-ad43-1ae35079f738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352018} :answer-field/id #uuid "69982ee7-0741-5c08-835f-b26951ee678f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "298d5629-725b-5aa5-9d76-4ed61398d66b" :question/math-academy-id "q-87802" :question/problem "![](images/37/3756b00cce29aad77b7a0b1ebb09f43cb89a602f8462edce89e8ba6346cb7fab.png)\n\nWhat is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Since $m∠A=m∠B$, we have an isosceles triangle, where $AC=BC.$\n\nHence, the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {10}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 100 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
